  "local_policy": "Independent one-point permanent cost grants listen only on actual starts of the current hand controller. They pause in deck, preserve ordinary stored/copy material, and reset with ordinary bounce/silence. An accepted tick requires its original grant to remain on the same continuous hand residence and controller. Ordinary transformation follows existing clearing semantics and removes the grant; no material is reinstalled for the tick. Grant copies remain independent. Generated minion carries its grant before the first creation/acquisition notification, including burned output. Carver uses the existing optional friendly-hand Battlecry target policy; empty-target behavior, exact zone/timing/copy rules and full legal pool require CN calibration. The forum empty-hand bug report has no authoritative rule confirmation and is not treated as calibration."
